The scene pauses briefly so the complete arrangement is clearly visible.

The same pair of feminine hands enters naturally from the lower edge of the frame.

The hands move toward the chosen garment with clear intention.

One hand grips the left side of the garment and the other hand grips the right side.

The grip must occur at structurally safe areas such as:

- shoulder edges;
- side seams;
- waistband corners;
- upper corners;
- reinforced edges;
- sleeve openings;
- stable fabric areas.

Do not grip the garment by:

- a fragile strap alone;
- a button;
- a zipper pull;
- embroidery;
- decorative applique;
- loose bow;
- delicate lace;
- thin drawstring;
- print;
- hard ornament.

