Use stable soft natural daylight.

Maintain accurate product colors.

No flicker.

No moving light source.

No changing white balance.

No orange shift.

No blue shift.

No artificial glow.

No exposure pumping as the garment approaches the camera.

Allow only natural physically correct shadow changes caused by the garment being lifted.

REALISM:

The movement must look like a real woman physically choosing one garment from a styled
fashion composition and bringing it close to the camera for inspection.

Show:

- realistic hand pressure;
- natural fingertip contact;
- believable garment weight;
- realistic fabric response;
- accurate textile fibers;
- natural folds;
- physically plausible movement;
- subtle room ambience;
- authentic smartphone product-video realism.

Do not create a floating garment.

Do not make the clothing move before being touched.

Do not animate the print.

Do not make the garment rigid like cardboard.

Do not make the fabric liquid, rubbery or weightless.

STRICT NEGATIVE CONSTRAINTS:

No looping.

No return to the first frame.

No repeated action.

No lowering the garment after lifting.

No second garment being selected.

No garment switching during the lift.

No garment transforming into another piece.

No product replacement.

No duplicated garment.

